namespace Erdos888

/-
# Problem Description

Erdős Problem 888. What is the size of the largest `A ⊆ {1, …, n}` such that whenever
`a ≤ b ≤ c ≤ d` lie in `A` and `abcd` is a square, `ad = bc`? `erdos_888` answers this: the
extremal size is `Θ(n · log log n / log n)`.

A question of Erdős, Sárközy and Sós [Er98, p.178]. Erdős reports that Sárközy proved
`|A| = o(n)`, and the primes give a lower bound. Below, `RequiredCondition A n` is the stated
property for `A ⊆ {1, …, n}`, `p n k` says an admissible `A` of cardinality `k` exists, and
`Nat.findGreatest (p n) n` is therefore the largest admissible size — the statement is that of
the Formal Conjectures entry verbatim. The lower bound uses primes and squarefree semiprimes;
the upper bound uses square-part fibres, a two-largest-prime encoding, a coloured rectangle
estimate and dyadic analytic bounds.

The formalisation is by plby (github.com/plby/lean-proofs),
`src/latest/ErdosProblems/Erdos888.lean` together with the modules of
`src/latest/ErdosProblems/Erdos888/`. Those files are concatenated here in dependency order,
with their project-internal imports removed so that `Mathlib` is the only import, each
module's contents kept in a `section` carrying its own `open` lines, and the whole wrapped
once in `namespace Erdos888` with the upstream trust-base print line removed. No mathematical
content is changed.
-/

